<title>CANADA: WCE president to resign at end of October.</title>
<headline>WCE president to resign at end of October.</headline>
<dateline>WINNIPEG 1996-10-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Fred Siemens, the president of the Winnipeg Commodity Exchange will resign his position at the end of October, the chairman of the WCE board of governors said.</p>
<p>&quot;This was quite a surprise when he announced it to the board of governors yesterday,&quot; WCE chairman Cornell Slade told reporters here.</p>
<p>Siemens became president of the WCE in March 1992 and will leave his post at the end of October to work with a joint venture company in Calgary specializing in electronic cash commodity brokerage, Slade said.</p>
<p>Siemens was not immediately available for comment.</p>
<p>-- Gilbert Le Gras 204 947 3548</p>
